      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am sorry this broke your test scripts. It is common to name the CMake build directory as \"build\". When the libaom source tree had a directory named \"build\", the CMake build directory needed to use a different name (such as \"build.aom\") or be created outside the libaom source tree.\n\nHere is the description of this change in the libaom v3.14.0 release notes:\n\n```\nThe `build` directory in the source tree was removed and the original\nbuild/cmake directory was moved up one level. If you use the CMake\ntoolchain files in the original build/cmake/toolchains directory,\nthey are now in the cmake/toolchains directory.\n```",
